59512056e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,32,37236,315,264,9861,41009,2248,374,264,1555,10238,20913,1378,2477,12,24739,18181,17228,13,2585,1657,84018,1127,1558,264,20189,23450,93610,614,30,508,6405,921,474,2326,280,2141,7,16,15,15,317,2258,2752,2333,258,28357,7,15,13,22,1106,3231,60471,284,29199,12679,4080,15,13,17,4999,16,11,17,14,18,626,1004,4038,47,306,6113,320,7951,305,340,4257,2343,18,379,401,88,4539,15,11,15,19806,29621,7,18,11,15,19806,29621,7,20,11,18,19806,29621,7,18,11,21,19806,29621,7,15,11,20,19806,29621,21621,401,7633,76850,7021,701,5782,10128,337,491,626,7633,7021,317,630,1004,4038,21095,7624,3778,264,11,23725,293,11,1931,305,340,4257,2343,18,379,401,88,24239,313,65,313,65,13362,15,11,15,19806,29621,64,13362,15,11,15,19806,29621,21621,401,7633,76850,7021,701,5782,11,11453,10128,337,491,317,630,7633,21095,1188,15,11,15,11,15,23547,15,11,20,11,15,701,19,317,7633,21095,1188,15,11,15,11,15,23547,18,11,15,11,15,701,19,317,7633,21095,1188,18,11,15,11,15,23547,20,11,18,11,15,701,19,317,7633,47,306,6113,7,19,626,322,474,2326,26,1482,60471,284,29199,12679,7,17,20,11,16,20,15,11,16,15,15,1215,442,2258,2752,2333,258,28357,7,15,13,23,5905,1379,7,16,15,15,317,322,1004,308,38,263,1548,1629,50,3341,11,1931,2608,1264,322,7951,9210,284,220,18,21,15,14,2413,50,3341,280,322,1958,1548,600,284,220,15,26,600,366,1629,50,3341,26,3443,72,1264,322,7633,14161,29633,23019,11,15,29621,3741,29633,6599,72,488,220,16,701,15,1106,322,7633,1188,3741,29633,23019,11,15,8,488,320,15,11,15,38709,593,313,7,3741,29633,6599,72,488,220,16,701,15,8,488,320,15,11,15,38709,4945,322,7633,14161,29633,23019,11,15,29621,7,3741,29633,23019,11,15,8,488,320,15,11,15,38709,4945,322,456,36323,322,77,38,263,7,20,11,17,317,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nA diagonal of a polyhedron is a line segment connecting two non-adjacent vertices. How many diagonals does a pentagonal prism have? [asy]\nimport three;\nsize(100);\ndefaultpen(linewidth(0.7));\ncurrentprojection = orthographic(-0.2,-1,2/3);\n\nvoid drawPentagon (real h)\n{\n\npath3 y;\n\ny=(0,0,h)--(3,0,h)--(5,3,h)--(3,6,h)--(0,5,h)--cycle;\n\ndraw(surface(y),white,nolight);\n\ndraw(y);\n}\n\nvoid drawRectangle(triple a, triple b, real h)\n{\n\npath3 y;\n\ny=a--b--b+(0,0,h)--a+(0,0,h)--cycle;\n\ndraw(surface(y),white,black,nolight);\n}\n\ndrawRectangle((0,0,0),(0,5,0),4);\ndrawRectangle((0,0,0),(3,0,0),4);\ndrawRectangle((3,0,0),(5,3,0),4);\ndrawPentagon(4);\n\n//import three; currentprojection = orthographic(25,150,100); //defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); size(100);\n//void nGon(int numSides, real height){\n//real angle = 360/numSides;\n//for(int i = 0; i < numSides; ++i){\n//draw(dir(angle*i,0)--dir(angle*(i + 1),0));\n//draw((dir(angle*i,0) + (0,0,height))--(dir(angle*(i + 1),0) + (0,0,height)));\n//draw(dir(angle*i,0)--(dir(angle*i,0) + (0,0,height)));\n// }\n//}\n//nGon(5,2);\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"9641e6cb4487ff8eb3c765f71689b11a3e46b8130bd3f79580d433c1bd63fdd0"},"seconds":9.280833721160889,"seed":1105291253798870058,"stop":"eos","text":"To determine the number of diagonals in a pentagonal prism, we'll first calculate the total number of vertices and then apply the formula for the number of diagonals in a polyhedron.\n\n### Step 1: Determine the Number of Vertices\nA pentagonal prism consists of two pentagonal bases and five rectangular lateral faces. Each pentagon has 5 vertices, and there are two such pentagons.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total vertices} = 5 + 5 = 10\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the Total Number of Line Segments\nThe total number of line segments connecting any two vertices of a polyhedron with \\( n \\) vertices is given by \\( \\binom{n}{2} \\), which is the number of ways to choose 2 vertices out of \\( n \\):\n\n\\[\n\\binom{10}{2} = \\frac{10 \\times 9}{2} = 45\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Subtract the Number of Edges\nA pentagonal prism has both the edges of the two pentagonal bases and the edges connecting corresponding vertices of the two bases. \n\n- Each pentagonal base has 5 edges.\n- There are 5 edges connecting corresponding vertices of the two bases.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total edges} = 5 + 5 + 5 = 15\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Subtract the Number of Edges from the Total Number of Line Segments\nThe number of diagonals is the total number of line segments minus the number of edges:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Number of diagonals} = 45 - 15 = 30\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{30}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{30}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"counting_and_probability:65"}
